female reproductive system. It is essential for the development of female secondary sexual characteristics and is commonly measured to evaluate the onset of puberty. In individuals with aromatase deficiency, estradiol levels are typically low, which can lead to various developmental issues. Overall, estradiol is a vital hormone in female health and development.", "HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO:HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO, or hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of sex hormones resulting from inadequate stimulation by the pituitary gland. This condition can be either congenital or acquired and often leads to delayed puberty due to the low levels of sex hormones.", "RETRASO CONSTITUCIONAL:Constitutional delay is a temporary condition in which a child grows and develops more slowly than peers but eventually catches up, often affecting the timing of puberty.", "CARIOTIPO:Karyotype is a test that examines the number and structure of chromosomes, used to identify genetic abnormalities that may affect puberty.", "SÍNDROME DE KALLMAN:El síndrome de Kallman es un trastorno genético que causa hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo y anosmia, resultando en retraso puberal y amenorrea primaria en varones y mujeres.", "SÍNDROME DE KLINEFELTER:El síndrome de Klinefelter es una condición genética que afecta a hombres, caracterizada por la presencia de un cromosoma X adicional. Esta anomalía cromosómica puede resultar en hipogonadismo, que se manifiesta como una disminución en la producción de hormonas sexuales, así como en un retraso en el desarrollo puberal. Además, el síndrome puede influir en el desarrollo físico y cognitivo de los varones, generando diversos problemas de salud. En resumen, el síndrome de Klinefelter es una condición que impacta tanto el desarrollo físico como el cognitivo en los hombres debido a la presencia de un cromosoma X extra.", "ANOSMIA:La anosmia es la pérdida del sentido del olfato, que puede ser un síntoma asociado con el síndrome de Kallman.", "CRIPTORQUIDIA:Cryptorchidism, also known as \"criptorquidia\" in Spanish, is a medical condition characterized by the failure of one or both testicles to descend into the scrotum. This condition can have implications for hormonal and pubertal development in males.", "ORQUIDOPEXIA:ORQUIDOPEXIA, also known as orchidopexy, is a surgical procedure designed to correct cryptorchidism, a condition where one or both testicles fail to descend into the scrotum. The procedure involves placing the undescended testicle into the scrotum, allowing for proper positioning and function. This intervention is crucial for the health and development of the testicles, as it helps prevent potential complications associated with cryptorchidism.", "RETARDO PUBERAL:El retraso puberal es una condición en la que el desarrollo físico y hormonal de un adolescente se retrasa en comparación con sus pares."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}